  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">KLIC (Korean digital-Learning Improvement Cooperation_Tanzania) Capacity Building Training Program for Core Educators in Dar es Salaam on Developing L</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to promote the digital transformation of education in Dar es Salaam, Tanzania, and to bridge the global education gap by establishing a customized training system that reflects the policies of the Ministry of Education of Tanzania and the needs of the education field.

The basic course focuses on strengthening the capacity of key teachers in general subjects to develop localized educational content that reflects inclusiveness, while the advanced course is operated in a direction that supports the design of curriculum at the national level.

In addition, a digital teacher community will be formed centered on teachers who have completed the training, promoting regional training and the development of educational content. It also aims to establish a sustainable digital education system through infrastructure support tailored to the local educational environment.</narrative>
  </description>
